WEBVTT

00:16:29.036 --> 00:16:33.156
the ways that our identities
are unique and meaningful

00:16:33.196 --> 00:16:35.676
outside of just being productive.

00:16:35.676 --> 00:16:37.956
DP: I know so many
women of color I interviewed

00:16:37.956 --> 00:16:40.276
who won't talk about what
they do on the weekends

00:16:40.316 --> 00:16:43.756
or won't share that they speak another
language or won't bring their art.

00:16:43.796 --> 00:16:46.276
That was one one Black women
who told me a long story

00:16:46.316 --> 00:16:49.236
about how she wanted to bring
all her Black art to the office,

00:16:49.276 --> 00:16:51.596
but she didn't want to highlight
her differences.

00:16:51.596 --> 00:16:54.956
And she had a real struggle about whether
or not she should share that.

00:16:54.956 --> 00:16:57.116
We need to shed things
that don't work for us,

00:16:57.156 --> 00:16:58.516
but we also need to remember

00:16:58.556 --> 00:17:01.476
that we actually get our power
from who we are and our lineage